{"command": "cd /testbed && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\np=\"specs/001-transactions/plan.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\n\n# 1) Summary: extend for milestone 2\nold_summary=s[s.index(\"## Summary\"):s.index(\"## Technical Context\")]\nnew_summary=\"\"\"## Summary\n\nAdd a new additive public type `TaggedCache(maxsize)` in a new module\n`src/cachetools/tagged.py`. It wraps the existing `cachetools.LRUCache`\nfor bounded LRU storage and layers tag bookkeeping on top so entries can\nbe invalidated by tag (single tag or many, any/all). Every stored value\nis deep-copied on input and on retrieval; `get` misses raise `KeyError`;\ntag input is validated strictly (finite iterable of strings, deduplicated,\ngenerators consumed once, bare strings and non-string entries rejected\nwith `ValueError` before any state change); `maxsize` must be a positive\ninteger excluding booleans; `resize` changes capacity safely (shrink\nevicts LRU, grow evicts nothing, failure preserves all state); the\n`maxsize` property reports the current capacity. All existing\ncachetools APIs remain untouched (no edits to existing modules).\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(old_summary,new_summary,1)\n\n# 2) Phase 0 pointer: add R8-R10\nold_p0=s[s.index(\"## Phase 0\"):s.index(\"## Phase 1\")]\nnew_p0=\"\"\"## Phase 0 — Research (see research.md)\n\nResolved items: (1) reuse `LRUCache` via its public mapping protocol\nrather than subclassing or poking at name-mangled internals; (2) tag\nindex design (`key -> frozenset`, `tag -> set(keys)`); (3) validation\nordering (validate tags before touching state); (4) `maxsize` validation\nrule; (5) Claim-A open item disposition (put-refresh adopted); (6)\n`invalidate_many` any/all set semantics with empty-removes-zero (R04);\n(7) `resize` mechanics: popitem-based shrink + capacity update, rebuild\nrejected (R05); (8) generator tags consumed exactly once (R06). Details\nand alternatives in [research.md](research.md).\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(old_p0,new_p0,1)\n\n# 3) Phase 1 pointer: mention milestone-2 additions\nold_p1=s[s.index(\"## Phase 1\"):s.index(\"## Complexity Tracking\")]\nnew_p1=\"\"\"## Phase 1 — Design (see data-model.md, contracts/, quickstart.md)\n\n- Entities and invariants (incl. resize transitions): [data-model.md](data-model.md)\n- Public API contract (incl. `invalidate_many`, `resize`, `maxsize`\n  property): [contracts/tagged-cache-api.md](contracts/tagged-cache-api.md)\n- Validation scenarios (incl. milestone-2 boundaries): [quickstart.md](quickstart.md)\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(old_p1,new_p1,1)\n\n# 4) Technical Context: append milestone-2 observed facts\nanchor=\"- Upstream tests: `tests/test_*.py` (13 files) must remain unmodified.\"\nadd=(anchor+\"\\n\"\n\"- `Cache` exposes a read-only `maxsize` property (observed, lines ~148-152)\"\n\"\\n  backed by the name-mangled `self.__maxsize` set in `Cache.__init__` — a\"\n\"\\n  runtime capacity change therefore either updates that attribute or\"\n\"\\n  rebuilds the LRU cache (see research.md R7).\"\n\"\\n- `LRUCache.popitem()` is a public method returning the LRU `(key, value)`\"\n\"\\n  pair (observed, lines 224-231) — usable for shrink-eviction without\"\n\"\\n  reaching into `__order`.\"\n\"\\n- `LRUCache.__iter__` inherits `Cache.__iter__` (plain dict, insertion\"\n\"\\n  order — NOT recency order, observed lines 126-128 + 208) — recency\"\n\"\\n  order is only observable via `popitem()`/eviction, so any reordering\"\n\"\\n  logic must use `popitem()`, not iteration.\")\ns=s.replace(anchor,add,1)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"plan.md updated, lines:\", s.count(chr(10)))\nPYEOF", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "plan.md updated, lines: 142\n"}